The Midnight name and logo are Midnight's trademarks. They are used here with
attribution, to say the Hall is built on the Midnight Network, unaltered and
under Midnight's brand guidelines. They are not licensed under Apache-2.0 or
any other license by this repository, and no right to use them is granted.

Files that contain Midnight's logo (the complete list, checked 2026-11-12):

- public/brand/midnight/Midnight-RGB_Symbol-White.svg
  (the official Midnight Logo Pack file 02_Symbol/Midnight-RGB_Symbol-White.svg,
  byte for byte; test/table-art.test.js and test/art.test.js check that)
- public/brand/midnight/Midnight-RGB_Logo-Horizontal-White.svg
  (the official Midnight Logo Pack file
  01_Symbol + Wordmark/Horizontal/Midnight-RGB_Logo-Horizontal-White.svg)
- public/og.jpg (the link preview image: the Midnight symbol is on the wall,
  left of the lantern)
- docs/the-hall-deck.pdf (its screenshots of the site show the Midnight
  symbol, e.g. on the shield above the door on page 1). The deck's own words
  and layout are Apache-2.0; the screenshots of the site in it are not.

Everywhere else the logo shows on the site, it is drawn at run time from the
two SVG files above: the Sealed Hand card backs (the "midnight" card back, set
by cardBack in public/js/hall-config.js and styled in public/css/inn.css, full
size and mini), the marks laid over the Hall's room and the Cup & Claim table
(public/js/room.js, public/js/dice.js, public/js/tapestry-mark.js), the
"Built on the Midnight Network" line in each page's footer, and the turning
symbol on a button that is waiting. The code that places them is Apache-2.0;
the mark it shows is not. Any screenshot or recording of the site that shows
those card backs, marks, footers or buttons shows Midnight's logo and is
excluded in the same way.

No other file in this repository contains Midnight's logo. Every image was
checked: the other card back (public/art/cards.png, public/art/back-mini.png)
is the Hall's own wax-seal hand, and the art in public/art and art-source has
no Midnight mark painted in.

